! post_main - the per-CPU POST sequence (run by the master, then by each slave
! via mp_run_with_target). NVRAM 0x1ff1 == 3 (MXCC and non-MXCC modules
! mixed) -> post_fail_mixed_modules. NVRAM 0x1ff2 == 2 -> %g4 |= 2 (print
! test names) and "<<< CPU_n on MBus Slot_m >>> IS RUNNING (MID = x)".
! Memory config (0x125c0), keyboard check, then the CPU suites by module
! type: 0x17 HyperSPARC suite (0x21790), 0x42 SuperSPARC-II suite (0x1fb84),
! then for all SuperSPARCs: MMU context table/context regs, TLB bit patterns,
! MMU flush, D-cache and I-cache RAM/PTAG/STAG, I-cache flush, flash clear,
! MXCC suite if an MXCC is present. Then the system tests: EMC, ECC, FPU,
! memory address pattern, interrupts, timers, MSI/IOMMU, DMA2/LANCE/ESP/PP,
! TOD. Each test returns %g3 != 0 on failure. Keyboard LEDs (cmd 0x0e) mark
! progress.

