! pending bit for this CPU (pa 0xf_f140_n004 = 0x8000), keep the context.
! Ross: flush, clear its regs 0x1100-0x1700, unless MCNTL bit 27 write ASI 6
! va 0/8/0x10/0x18 (PTEs 0xff00003b/0xff00403b = PROM pa 0xff0000000 and
! 0xff0040000, tags 0xffd00000/0xffd40000, then again with tags 0/0x40000),
! flush the I-cache, and enter OBP at 0x54ff4 with the MMU on. Viking: caches/MMU off (MCNTL &= ~0x4301); unless
! MCNTL bit 27, dump PTP0/PTP2/PTP2-tag and all 64 D-TLB entries (ASI 6
! sel 0-3) to NVRAM 0x1cd8.. for the post-mortem.

