! OBP support code in C / assembler, linked in front of the Forth kernel
! (0x3d120-0x3e5ff, runs at VA 0xffd3xxxx): cache flush and init used by the
! reset path, a 64-bit memory test with SIMM (J-number) error reports, a small
! printf, and the romvec - the SPARC V2/V3 PROM interface an OS calls (struct
! linux_romvec at 0x3d580) - with its C wrappers that enter the Forth kernel
! under a per-CPU lock (romvec_enter/romvec_exit).

