! romvec_cpustart(cpu_node, &ctx_table_pa, context, pc) - v3_cpustart, how an OS
! starts a secondary CPU: under the PROM lock find the target's index / MID
! from the CPU table at 0xffef2008 + 16n; refuse (return -1) for itself or an
! unknown node. Set its bit in the started mask ([0xffef0670]), post
! [0xffef204c] = CTPR value (pa[35:32] << 28 | pa[31:0] >> 4), [0xffef2048] =
! context, [0xffef2050] = pc, [0xffef2004] = MID | 0xffff0000, then wait up to
! 100000 loops for the target's state byte ([0xffef04dc] + index) to read
! 0xf0. The target, spinning in the Forth word >idle-cpu-loop, takes the
! request and leaves through cpu_enter_client (0x274ac). Returns 0 / -1
! (state word 0xffef2010 + 16n = 0xf0 / 0x90).

